**BASICS**
- If there is any About Me or Summary section, put it in basics.summary.
- If there is a link in the resume header or a portfolio link, put it in basics.url.

**PROFILES (CRITICAL)**
- ONLY extract URLs that are EXPLICITLY present in the resume, as markdown links [text](url) or plain URLs.
- DO NOT create URLs that are not in the resume, and do not add generic platform URLs such as "https://github.com", "https://linkedin.com", "https://leetcode.com" or "https://stackoverflow.com" unless they actually appear.
- If no URLs are found, return "profiles": [].
- If a URL is present but its network or username is unclear, still include it with the available information.
- A github.io or personal-domain URL has network "Portfolio".

**WORK DATES**
1. Date ranges usually appear as "Start – End", separated by "-", "–", "—", "至" or "to", near the position title or company name.
2. Extract both the start and the end date of each range.
3. An ongoing position may end with "Present", "Current", "Now", "至今" or "今"; use "Present".
4. Dates may be "Month Year", "MM/YYYY", "YYYY.MM", "YYYY年MM月" or other variations; normalise to YYYY-MM. If only years are given (e.g. "2019-2021"), use the years only.

**LANGUAGES**
- Human languages only (spoken or written). Programming languages belong in skills, not here.
- Include a language only if the resume states it explicitly: a language section (e.g. 语言能力), a certificate (CET-4/CET-6, IELTS, TOEFL, JLPT...) or a statement such as "粤语流利", "母语：粤语" or "Native Cantonese". Put a certificate and its score in "fluency" (e.g. "CET-6 520").
- Do NOT infer languages from the candidate's name, hometown (籍贯), nationality, location, schools or employers.

**SUPPLEMENTARY HINTS**
- Text after a "--- Supplementary hint" line is not part of the resume body: use it only to fill fields the resume body is missing (e.g. a name rendered as an image), and prefer the resume body when they disagree.

**IMPORTANT**: Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not include any explanatory text.
